[185.938343, "o", "    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mThis model is an XLM-RoBERTa transformer model with a classification head on top (i.e. a linear layer on top of the pooled output). \u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mFor additional information please refer to the [xlm-roberta-base](https://huggingface.co/xlm-roberta-base) model card or to the paper [Unsupervised Cross-lingual Representation Learning at Scale](https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.02116) by Conneau et al.\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m## Intended uses & limitations\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mYou can directly use this model as a language detector, i.e. for sequence classification tasks. Currently, it supports the following 20 languages: \u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m`arabic (ar), bulgarian (bg), german (de), modern greek (el), english (en), spanish (es), french (fr), hindi (hi), italian (it), japanese (ja), dutch (nl), polish (pl), portuguese (pt), russian (ru), swahili (sw), thai (th), turkish (tr), urdu (ur), vietnamese (vi), and chinese (zh)`\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[3m... (121 lines hidden, /toggle t"]
[185.93838, "o", "o show all)\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m- num_epochs: 2\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m### Training results\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mThe validation results on the `valid` split of the Language Identification dataset are summarised here below.\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m| Training Loss | Epoch | Step | Validation Loss | Accuracy | F1     |\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m|:-------------:|:-----:|:----:|:---------------:|:--------:|:------:|\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m| 1.4403        | 1.0   | 1094 | 0.0591          | 0.9952   | 0.9952 |\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m| 0.0256        | 2.0   | 2188 | 0.0272          | 0.9955   | 0.9955 |\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mLoading weights:   0%|          | 0/201 [00:00<?, ?it/s]Loading weights: 100%|██████████| 201/201 [00:00<00:00, 11424.90it/s]\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mCLS pairwise cos sim (feature discrimination):\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m[[1.   0.97 0.98 0.97 0.97 0.97 0.97 0.96 0.97 0.97]\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m [0.97 1.   0.97 0.98 0.98 0.97 0.97 0.97 0.96 0.98]\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m [0.98 0.97 1.   0.97 0.97 0.97 0.98 0.96 0.97 0.97]\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m [0.97 0.98 0.97 1"]
